1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
A key in the code, in the app, on forty thousand phones.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,200
He unzipped the app. It took him a minute.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,200
He does not delete anything. He just uses it.

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,200
One click at three in the morning. The bleeding stops.

5
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:14,200
Every installed copy carries the key you just revoked.

6
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,200
New build, store review, and then people have to update.

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,000
If the key had lived in Key Vault, rotation changes nothing for users.

8
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,800
If fixing it needs an app store release, it was never a secret.
